tion-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/d550ecec3b7103c9510b6e45e738ae1385e07fa63ff2e50c54da6c17606faaec.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in {-3,-2,-1},\\,y\\in {-4,-3,-2,-1}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe8d7e2-7a00-5a6c-9c30-2f82cc2512fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312960} {:answer/id #uuid "06bfec6b-1d54-539b-8758-ca0b41383b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312961} {:answer/id #uuid "04e2abc6-61d4-5107-8338-1beaa4753837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312962} {:answer/id #uuid "f73bb3a6-b5d8-5a45-a5ed-d5d5e2e2cad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312963} {:answer/id #uuid "0c09b59d-5ea2-58bc-b97b-7f898134b98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312964} {:answer/id #uuid "fccbee1b-8d24-5ecc-939a-6738ca80f4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe8d7e2-7a00-