} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "885684e2-c25b-548a-83cd-7595b3cbc61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313008} :answer-field/id #uuid "db295b5d-653a-5a1d-96cc-e9483679756e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eda92421-f224-560a-bf64-d4c99cd32f4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-181679" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/718ee39f4a0b2e9cca18ed4de77271a90139b13e8b71990611c1e13357245713.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-x+5,\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=-x+5$ and *below* the line $y=x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<-x+5,\\,y<x+3.\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<-x+5,\\,y<x+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e97f100-9a3e-5689-9815-78204f49e79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313011} {:answer/id #uuid "075c0b5b-f8e9-5ec7-a79f-4c0606238509" :