{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-2<y<\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=-2$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n-2\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517cde0f-a020-59b5-b37a-804548b2826f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313030} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8b1dcd-1510-55ae-add0-7cd0ce9d1517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313031} {:answer/id #uuid "41589387-c8b1-5857-8fd2-e305f0cf3ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313032} {:answer/id #uuid "518a4e21-8195-5247-9eee-2a6e9865ae79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313033} {:answer/id #uuid "319c5a85-9877-5a84-81ce-eab67aad58ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "517cde0f-a020-59b5-b37a-804548b2826f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313030} :answer-field/id #uuid "63cbd75e-3c3d-5d91-aa72-61bb4e9f6bba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8b