 :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313121} :answer-field/id #uuid "270824ad-a788-5ff8-be8f-763b9c5e3552" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313120} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67c279bc-3cbd-52d6-ae90-f27994165e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313124} {:answer/id #uuid "883cbbe3-8ae8-5890-bb6a-177ffc845180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "883cbbe3-8ae8-5890-bb6a-177ffc845180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313125} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5c2df8-4e7f-510b-a801-3e31d2c1e88c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bed9f134-b957-5dc6-9472-e71f383e3d77" :question/math-academy-id "q-181804" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/a87b00f9f7908fe62542ef7bca94277f040af97b4af24698dd648c167bcd3376.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\,{{field-1}}\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,5,\\,2\\,{{field-3}}\\,y\\,{{field-4}}\\,5}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the rectangle if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1<x<5,\\,2<y<5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we also need to *include* the bottom edge ($y=2$).\n\nTherefore, we change the corresponding inequality symbol to non-strict, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1<x<5,\\,2\\le y<5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<x<5,\\,2\\le y<5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cceb13e4-ac2f-5521-b32b-6215f4e5f108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313128} {:answer/id #uuid "3d107d4c-b4e5-5f02-8331-bc8f430f5951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cceb13e4-ac2f-5521-b32b-6215f4e5f108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313128} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bd676ca-9eaf-5557-9bd2-715c998879c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67dad6f4-a6ca-50d8-9c85-40e846b23429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313131} {:answer/id #uuid "a586a876-f95f-5f88-b7f9-34e041001364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a586a876-f95f-5f88-b7f9-34e041001364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313132} :answer-field/id #uuid "b20d037e-1d27-5525-bf48-07da2fe14849" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9082c766-1bb5-5c2f-9b03-28a47e32ca5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313134} {:answer/id #uuid "57332d9b-653e-5414-a9cb-42649f70cf11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57332d9b-653e-5414-a9cb-42649f70cf11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313135} :answer-field/id #uuid "13d53cde-b3f6-5fa1-8adc-3e0278a50e78" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "734e0047-51aa-5137-b11a-92a9e6d42f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313137} {:answer/id #uuid "664a10e5-3ce5-550c-a9d7-846c1b7088fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "664a10e5-3ce5-550c-a9d7-846c1b7088fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313138} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dfd3fb1-bf04-5acd-bc87-28038196ea05" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06624e01-3e0b-5189-ac4c-e6d2964b1400" :question/math-academy-id "q-181806" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/a659e2d14a645036488833cd920e6bb3e3d7a7716724dba63814be6df4066fe9.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,{{field-1}}\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,6,\\,-1\\,{{field-3}}\\,y\\,{{field-4}}\\,4}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the rectangle if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3<x<6,\\,-1<y<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we also need to *include* the left edge ($x=3$).\n\nTherefore, we change the corresponding inequality symbol to non-strict, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\le x<6,\\,-1<y<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\le x<6,\\,-1<y<4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f450c047-e61e-5202-a9d7-5dec1755ad5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313141} {:answer/id #uuid "bb105375-3a73-5ff1-989b-a3fd473cbc1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313142} {:answer/id #uuid "3a963cbb-df45-5309-8299-166a9b5a6954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313143} {:answer/id #uuid "f563bb43-8b8f-56ad-af70-2addcca6f79a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f450c047-e61e-5202-a9d7-5dec1755ad5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313141} :answer-field/id #uuid "737a7821-7523-5d22-86f7-a10c5ad64d90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "917c637a-e2cf-58ad-91b7-9041a7346f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313146} {:answer/id #uuid "b78c198a-bce7-55b5-9b71-28e1075fa5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313147} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b2a731-6fea-5993-8a0f-9ea7e0dd9247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313148} {:answer/id #uuid "05de3ffa-3948-53fc-b935-dbcff9765caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313149} {:answer/id #uuid "19d8b18a-3ad5-5e33-99c2-78f3532d3083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d8b18a-3ad5-5e33-99c2-78f3532d3083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313150} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fab2ce5-84ed-54ae-b1b0-f776d64e95cf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf93bafd-c531-5005-a89e-494f2be67c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-181807" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/8c23fe5aa17b46293ff29cd8621ee10b2e143cb23b77811ddf20037a1639bce0.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,{y}^{2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *to the left* of the curve $x={y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx<{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the curve is dashed), the inequality is strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x<{y}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907144ab-1571-5ad9-9d62-f1a0d4895464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313153} {:answer/id #uuid "b07ebc6d-af67-5434-965c-c3a53de55979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313154} {:answer/id #uuid "f32ed7d7-5c25-51b4-b504-f0007fd41016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313155} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb6faa4-71a4-5afb-abea-771e51bafcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "907144ab-1571-5ad9-9d62-f1a0d4895464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313153} :answer-field/id #uuid "79f6d23b-e63e-5419-9dd6-8037aba92787" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92d2955-ffc3-59fe-a0f9-fe19247a90fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313158} {:answer/id #uuid "890a299d-06bc-57e0-a3ce-9a054cabee6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313159} {:answer/id #uuid "7f6b6f4e-7c48-548d-8647-1c5596afdd34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313160} {:answer/id #uuid "f7643e29-bd35-5c95-a2e0-16e404cfb3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313161} {:answer/id #uuid "11510cac-2187-52ff-8d60-23e0a7882361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7643e29-bd35-5c95-a2e0-16e404cfb3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313161} :answer-field/id #uuid "453c6eb2-37f8-57ba-b4dd-4963be0e92f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a69b369-bbb1-51a1-a0c6-42cc01864162" :question/math-academy-id "q-181808" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/664c70223ca8a6219b04a287c779d20bf0f88d770920d1357303721574d90787.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,{x}^{2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe must also include the curve $y={x}^{2}$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge {x}^{2}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge {x}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36fa0f2f-3812-521a-aca3-900556be84ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Non-Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a06aeb8-ebbf-5be2-aa81-046f5ec144b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a06aeb8-ebbf-5be2-aa81-046f5ec144b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313165} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dcfd8f0-cd57-5eae-b02b-1ceb6aec28bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc62fef-e865-5ef2-af53-3ed9aba4c018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cc62fef-e865-5ef2-af53-3ed9aba4c018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313167} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ed1374-c069-5d94-93d3-448c33b038ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f846df1-067e-51fc-ad78-1627373ac119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f846df1-067e-51fc-ad78-1627373ac119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313169} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b083f2b-befa-55c2-bf5a-678e6148376c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b0ab361-6cc4-50f5-a263-8b645cd23440" :question/math-academy-id "q-181809" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/8be62d80165b756aedf31e998d6636d7f77a5606e195b3ec288cb0ac6fb52d6f.png)\n\nUse set builder notation to describe the shaded region given in the diagram above:\n\n${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n${y}^{2}$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$144$\n\n$}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the elliptical boundary of our region has horizontal radius $a=4$ and vertical radius $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}=144.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in describing all points that lie *outside* the ellipse. So, let's pick any point outside the region, say, $(0,4).$ Substituting its coordinates into the equation of the boundary, we obtain\n\n$$\n9(0)^{2}+16(4)^{2}\\,>\\,144.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the points $P(x,y)$ in our region are any real numbers that satisfy the condition\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}>144.\n$$\n\nNotice that we use $>$ since the boundary is excluded from the set (the boundary curve is dashed).\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,9{x}^{2}+16{y}^{2}>144}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, One Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f509ce1b-67e5-51bc-beba-08a2ee6e05ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313172} {:answer/id #uuid "7336015d-180c-52f4-bd6b-b93a95c068bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313173} {:answer/id #uuid "664e96ad-f223-5e9e-8006-0132ad80c67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313174} {:answer/id #uuid "5a0c26e9-aa2e-580d-b259-e5948ed3cd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313175} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0218fd-0042-5231-bd4d-a9a816216f0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313176} {:answer/id #uuid "ea69fb5e-da6b-5c02-9e0c-dc9468c557e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a0c26e9-aa2e-580d-b259-e5948ed3cd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313175} :answer-field/id #uuid "a91355f0-1594-52f0-a585-dc57f7f49481" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b8b8596-9d59-595f-9a05-bf533dedcd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313179} {:answer/id #uuid "41551095-0aef-5a21-88e5-ceae86bf8551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313180} {:answer/id #uuid "870c42bc-68b1-5949-82e0-ca5ac728af0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313181} {:answer/id #uuid "23a7a9ee-1e62-5820-ae10-e98c796bad9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313182} {:answer/id #uuid "1f161290-f298-5050-a6c6-369c17edd8e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23a7a9ee-1e62-5820-ae10-e98c796bad9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313182} :answer-field/id #uuid "55fe9a80-4cbe-5c87-9157-68917a7de008" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0486dc3-5d9e-5f68-9cf5-938a2bd521f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-181970" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/010d4befaa2bd2142cf63010f79f071df331bb6394eb65e4f883752cb04a2cb4.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,-x+1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x+1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x+1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, One Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76c29f15-1080-5e3a-a20b-be91388263dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313186} {:answer/id #uuid "d502614d-6309-5e3a-b19c-12361f1cf5d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313187} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e3a524-7c0d-5dde-b595-71331523c0f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313188} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b90094-1047-5752-91b9-893e454a7aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c29f15-1080-5e3a-a20b-be91388263dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313186} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c572e3-9742-5619-9c3c-56b4a8aa3343" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46fea0be-b0eb-5e25-9382-d2888315f038" :answer/type {:db/