x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>-x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, One Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68cc777-e5a8-5f7f-943d-7962fa7afd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195442} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e26431-e624-5007-a258-63e93fa31640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195443} {:answer/id #uuid "231f54d2-5353-560b-86cc-2881e48694ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195444} {:answer/id #uuid "3882d344-8e09-5098-9081-10beebe42927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195445} {:answer/id #uuid "60b15d59-218a-57bd-93be-97a0eea1adf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195446} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2bcd9d-3a4d-5dc9-bdea-14491a5f5e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "231f54d2-5353-560b-86cc-2881e48694ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195444} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe672945-dcce-5d71-9139-e2995ec7a8ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8051a7e-cc99-5656-aff3-3160671276b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≠" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195449} {:answer/id #uuid "b630a8cb-3982-52bf-b8d1-b72e141248af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195450} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc97330-990e-5af8-a9d2-e675280bd1b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≥" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195451} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b36bb3-c4bf-5a71-a3d2-c0d8d3f97a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≤" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195452} {:answer/id #uuid "f73cedd6-1762-5543-8c2e-afd38a3f8c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b630a8cb-3982-52bf-b8d1-b72e141248af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195450} :answer-field/id #uuid "94808da5-b051-5604-92e7-c95eee635654" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186195448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8574c8b5-4403-5982-8ea8-0dec7fa70982" :question/math-academy-id "q-181983" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/cce16725dddcfc83098ee2323576b8e01bbc3f2625d17cb7e6030826ad9fbcd8.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,x-1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=x-1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<x-1\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny<x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y<x-1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186313196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2